sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 436 µm on Holocene Felis catus (pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 87.6/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the Holocene nominal point (k* = 6.135, simulated wavelength 431.3 µm versus the 436 µm slot scale). A linearised spectral integration of sigma(k) matches the analytic dispersion with Pearson r = 0.990, RMSE 0.370, KS 0.111. Raising inhibitor diffusivity Dv from 0.55 to 3.20 lengthens lambda monotonically (Pearson r = 0.984). Equal diffusion and deletion of the u^2 v term both collapse the pattern. The segmented specimen is non-circular (circularity 0.146, aspect 1.37, foreground 0.30). Isotropic kinetics select a spot lattice; Dy/Dx = 4 raises the orientation anisotropy from 0.02 to 0.59 and produces stripes. Felis chronoseries is 1/1 at 0 Ma: an 80 µm cellular domain is stable, and a 4360 µm flank holds ten repeats of the same wave. Overall 87.6/100 (faithfulness 86.7, reproducibility 89.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/felis_catus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 614649 B, 1496×902 px, artifact_sha256 23f064546c3b921273e0aa9cc1fc8f324dfd31182e4201d1c8c83a3e4dc15fe7 (sha256 23f064546c3b921273e0aa9cc1fc8f324dfd31182e4201d1c8c83a3e4dc15fe7), spec_fingerprint dc73277e26df9e4f2f17850cccebf7acc56dadcc0fc11952482db451621788f3. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: dc73277e26df9e4f2f17850cccebf7acc56dadcc0fc11952482db451621788f3; artifact_sha256: 23f064546c3b921273e0aa9cc1fc8f324dfd31182e4201d1c8c83a3e4dc15fe7; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/felis_catus_turing_wavelength_s0/felis_catus_specimen.jpg=9360be6f1689a1df..., datasets/felis_catus_turing_wavelength_s0/felis_catus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=a7694c1c70d27f08...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-felis-catus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: instability at a finite wavenumber can produce stationary chemical waves. | Murray 1981: coat pre-pattern repeat count tracks domain size divided by the chemical wavelength. | Kaelin 2012: Taqpep establishes the fetal cat pre-pattern; Edn3 implements pigment. | Kaelin 2021: Dkk4 marks the fetal epidermal pre-pattern before stripes are visible.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg linearisation, spectral integration, Dv sweep, and two simulated ablations. | Physical calibration lambda(k*) = 436 µm at one Holocene parameter point. | Body-mask segmentation of the CC BY-SA photograph and a Dy/Dx stripe probe.; transfer_boundary: Schnakenberg rates are not Dkk4 or Wnt biochemical constants. | The adult photograph is not a 436 µm micrograph. The spot lattice is the isotropic law; mackerel stripes need anisotropy the genes have not been shown to set.; does_not_claim: That Kaelin, Murray, or Turing measured 436 µm. | That the phenotype panel is a pixel-fitted fetal skin simulation. | A second Felis chronospecies. The series is Holocene only, age 0 Ma.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R-assessor', 'item': 'Still a single builder-assessor. An independent second assessor was not run.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R-micrograph', 'item': 'No 436 µm fetal-skin micrograph. The adult CC photograph is the phenotype carrier, and 436 µm remains the slot scale rather than a Kaelin caliper value.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R-n1', 'item': 'Segmentation and image fitness use one individual (Von.grzanka 2010).'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.876"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; no second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

